Overlay patch 0032: aspect-aware object cull cone (the blinking fix).

is_within_render_distance culls actors/billboards by yaw angle around the
camera: extended_fov = fov * 0xB6 * scaleFov, scaleFov hardcoded 1.25 —
tuned for a narrow aspect. The iPhone renders 2736x1260 (2.17:1): the
screen's horizontal FOV exceeds the cull cone, so edge-visible billboards
(trees, palms) are culled WHILE ON SCREEN and pop back next tick as the
camera yaw wobbles — the user-visible "trees blinking when turning",
video-reproduced on sim (artifacts/blink-video/race-real.mp4 frames
83-85: tree present/absent/present; 145 flicker events in 30 s).

Fix: widen the cone, live-tunable via gSohIos.CullFovScalePct (default 300,
the A/B-tested value: 88 flicker events at upstream 1.25 vs 36 at 3.00,
matched parked-camera segments, 2026-07-21). Cost of over-wide: a few extra
off-screen objects drawn — noise on Metal. 0 disables the override
(upstream 1.25). Verification: same video harness; pass = flicker events
collapse to ~0.


--- a/src/racing/math_util.c
+++ b/src/racing/math_util.c
@@ -1113,6 +1113,20 @@
     maxDistance *= 6.5f;
     maxDistance2 = 1.0f;
     scaleFov = 1.25;
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0032): 1.25 is tuned for a narrow aspect; at the
+    // phone's 2.17:1 the screen's horizontal FOV exceeds the cull cone, so
+    // edge-visible billboards are culled while on screen — the "blinking
+    // trees" (video-reproduced: artifacts/blink-video frames 83-85).
+    // Live-tunable for A/B; 0 restores upstream.
+    {
+        extern s32 CVarGetInteger(const char* name, s32 defaultValue);
+        s32 sohIosCullPct = CVarGetInteger("gSohIos.CullFovScalePct", 300);
+        if (sohIosCullPct > 0) {
+            scaleFov = sohIosCullPct / 100.0f;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
 
     f32 extended_fov = ((f32) fov * 0xB6 * scaleFov); // Sets the Culling for objects on the left and right
 
